module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.fail_closed_gate_refuses_its_own_repair

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data fail_closed_gate_refuses_its_own_repair: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "fail_closed_gate_refuses_its_own_repair" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a fail-closed gate predicates evaluation on base-revision health and therefore refuses the change that restores that health.** INVALID STATE: the gate correctly declines to compare an unreadable base, but has no representable arm for `the base defect is exactly the subject this change removes`. Its safety property becomes self-sealing: every ordinary change is rightly refused while the repair is refused for the same reason, so no gate-admitted transition can restore the precondition the gate requires.",
    "MEASURED SPECIMEN (2026-09-04): gunbc#10390 left an unattached `//` block at the tail of `dag/test/claim/emit_copy_qualification_witness_test.dag`; the base revision then failed parsing with 16 diagnostics. On gunbc#10428, which moved that block onto a declaration and made the file parse again, the namespace-wave-admission phase reported `NotEvaluated -- dag/test/claim/emit_copy_qualification_witness_test.dag does not parse at the base revision (16 diagnostic(s)), so its base-side declarations cannot be read`. The refusal was correct, and #10428 could repair main only because it landed despite that refusal. Its next run was green.",
    "SECOND MEASURED SPECIMEN (2026-09-10), same class, different file: gunbc#10630 added `dag/gunbc/machine_intake/megarac_media_attach.dag` with three annotation blocks in declaration bodies; the base revision then failed parsing with 17 diagnostics, and every main head from 523657c15cc onward was red. On gunbc#10932, which hoists those blocks to module-item grain and makes the file parse again, the parse phase reported `parse OK 5391 file(s) parse-clean` while namespace-wave-admission reported `NotEvaluated -- dag/gunbc/machine_intake/megarac_media_attach.dag does not parse at the base revision (17 diagnostic(s)), so its base-side declarations cannot be read`. Same self-sealing shape, six days after the first specimen, with the trigger still unfired.",
    "THE SECOND SPECIMEN ADDS A COMPOUNDING FACT THE FIRST DID NOT SHOW: an aborted phase bounds the error total behind it. Parse refused before exhaustiveness was ever asked, so a genuine non-exhaustive match that #10630 introduced in a second file -- `fleet_account_key_label` in `gunbc.machine_intake.boot_image_export_ownership` matching seven arms of an eight-variant `FleetPosixAccountKey` -- was invisible on main for the whole outage and became reachable only once the parse repair was applied. So the outage this class extends also conceals its own scope: the count of defects the base carries is not observable while the base cannot be read, and a repair author who reports `main is fixed` on the strength of one phase going quiet will be wrong.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: nothing widened, defaulted, or fabricated, so this is NOT `absorbing_fallback`; the gate preserved ignorance as NotEvaluated exactly as fail-closed requires. The defect is transition reachability, not verdict truth. Recognition rule: for every gate that requires a healthy base, construct a base violating that precondition and a head differing only by removal of the violation; if the same refusal covers both that repair and an unrelated change, the gate has no repair discriminator and its invariant is self-sealing.",
    "HARM: a below-floor parse defect on main made its own direct repair unmergeable by the required admission mechanism, and every other pull request inherited the refusal until an operator used a route outside that mechanism. A gate intended to bound change thereby extended the outage and required an unmodeled exception at the moment its guarantee mattered most.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable by operator inspection and exceptional landing, with the invalid transition still writable and no mechanism distinguishing it. CEILING: mechanically preventable, not structural today: admitting a purported repair from the head alone is the obvious fail-open trap, because an ordinary change can conceal, relocate, or replace the unreadable base subject while claiming repair. A safe arm must establish both a bounded defect identity on the base and monotone removal of only that defect without pretending to compare base semantics the parser could not produce. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: a revision-scoped recovery-parse and change-classification capability sufficient to locate a bounded base defect in raw source, prove that the head removes that same defect, and prove that no outside-scope semantic change rides with it; the gate may then admit only that typed Repair transition while continuing to refuse every unclassified NotEvaluated change.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
